		new CrucibleGuideFight("Lauda Piece","Boss",new string[1] { "Lauda Piece" },new int[3] { 25, 32, 13 },new string[5] { "Many moves carry over from the Guttler Piece fight; the differences are Thunderbolt's stacking damage buff and the extra Deadly Demesne variation. Knowing all the attacks matters more than memorising a timeline. Without paralysis resistance, or when low on HP, have a pet tank Thunderbolt and swap it out for the next pet.", "Remember the Vanishing Daggers order before they vanish. Point Maker: avoid hitting the side statues.", "Unseen Force: a dagger in your back knocks you forward, one in your front knocks you back when the debuff expires. Combined with her Gluttonous attacks, stand with her and position to be knocked back. If it is Gutting (where you need to be with her), gap close afterwards and stand behind her; if it is Goring, ride the knockback to the other cubby to be safe.", "Deadly Demesne with circular daggers looks scary but is not bad: look at the two squares drawn in two corners, stand in a corner on the opposite diagonal to drop Molten Metal, then move away after the AoEs go off.", "When she starts Greater Strength, kill the two swords and note what she is casting: either be close to be knocked to a cubby, or go far to a cubby to avoid the proximity damage. Afterwards it repeats until dead and gets hectic the longer it goes." },Array.Empty<string>()) {
